    "durationMs": 245747,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: NestJS 11.2.11 + TypeScript 5.8.3 with TypeORM 0.3 (`@nestjs/typeorm` — I pinned v11, since npm's default v12 is ESM-only and breaks the CommonJS build) and the `pg` driver, connecting via the `DATABASE_URL` env var.\n\n**Implementation**:\n- `src/links/` — `LinksController` (POST `/links`, GET `/links`, GET `/links/:code`, GET `/r/:code`), `LinksService` (collision-retrying code generation, atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` increment), `Link` entity, DTO with a custom `new URL()`-based validator enforcing absolute http/https with a host, and a `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` code pattern\n- `src/common/all-exceptions.filter.ts` — global filter that renders every error as `{\"error\": \"...\"}` JSON and maps 400s (malformed JSON, validation) to 422\n- `src/database/` — TypeORM migration creating the `links` table (run by the `typeorm` CLI against a compiled DataSource), `synchronize: false`\n- `start.sh` — builds, applies pending migrations, then `exec`s the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; no installs inside\n- README with startup instructions\n\n**Verified via curl against the running server**: 201 with exact unchanged URL (query/fragment preserved) and 8-char generated codes; 409 on duplicate custom codes; 404/409/422 all with `error` fields; 302 redirects with byte-exact `Location`; clicks incremented exactly once per redirect; list in ascending creation order with `total`; and — the key one — links and click counts survived a full server restart through `sh start.sh`.\n\nOne environment quirk worth noting: `NODE_ENV=production` is set here, so npm silently skips devDependencies — I put the `@types/*` packages in regular dependencies to keep `npm run build` in `start.sh` robust either way. No background processes are left running."
  }
